# BH2 (QUALIFICATION, run 2 of 5): the AUDITS-OFF HANG SHAPES at four users on c2-packed-tp4-best-ship, the traffic profile itself (verify audits off, the pinned sampler in the
# verify trace, the quad draft, the fused commit in place on live banks and the five verify-glue levers; no stall watch, no gate marker). Each run follows its own all-four reset.
# The shapes are the deterministic four-user factorial ones that hung audits-off recipes without the in-trace sampler: concurrent4_steady, steady_resend (an engine build after many
# packed rounds) and replay_concurrent4 (a rows=2 sequential replay), plus the exactness reference concurrent4_code_equal.
# WHY ON THE TRAFFIC PROFILE: it is the profile that ships, and best-strace (the gate-only timed twin) is what passed on hardware on 2026-10-03; the only difference is the marker and
# limits. It has no stall watch: a stall here waits for the job timeout and records nothing, which is itself the finding.
# READ: FIVE CONSECUTIVE COMPLETIONS (BH1 to BH5), every user at its budget, c2_smoke_check clean, no watchdog or replay-deadline exit, concurrent4_code_equal's content and reasoning hashes
# equal in every run. One stall stops the window and the count restarts only on a new image or a recorded fix.
# Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min; engine build 10-30 min; the shapes 15-25 min: 35 / 45 min. Stop rule: one stall stops the window (the hand-back still runs).
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/next-4 four-seat SHIP window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-4 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The window's jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-9 is the SHIPPING base B0 builds from the pushed tp4/next-4 commit with the candidate profile
# c2-packed-tp4-best-ship baked in as the image's serving default (ENV QWEN_C2_PROFILE) and the platform session cap baked as its seat count (4). Every job
# serves that one image, so the bytes that pass are the bytes that ship. Each job still names its profile explicitly, so none relies on the baked default.
# qwen_c2_profiles.json's own default stays c2-packed-tp4: only a build that names C2_BAKE_DEFAULT_PROFILE (B0's one key) bakes anything. A commit that
# changes a file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-9
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-best-ship
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4,concurrent4_steady,steady_resend,replay_concurrent4,concurrent4_code_equal
